19_3985695.htm"}],"generated_at":"2026-09-08T16:02:26Z","limitations":["Changes and availability are observations from one outside-China collection vantage; they do not establish censorship, motive or an actor.","Indexes rotate normally. A link leaving an index does not establish that its document was removed.","Repeated 404/410 responses identify observed URL absence after a successful capture; access limits, redirects and transport errors stay separate.","Numeric-token changes are document differences, not normalized economic series revisions or evidence of fabricated statistics.","Historical methodology cases are attributed official announcements captured later; they are not changes first observed by this watch.","Public output contains original acquisition metadata and editorial summaries; source bodies and numeric tokens remain in the private evidence store."],"method_version":"official-publication-watch.v1","methodology_cases":[{"capture_ids":["60e8746e16bcb26db496d21cdbf507fd0da6ec2634f352c233fe6d7c60d9bef1","a287c2a866e46e54e52cfe61db82c306c1218246455f5b3fdff64455da5e90e5"],"claim":"NBS announced an age-group unemployment publication suspension in August 2023. In January 2024 it announced age-group rates excluding students and a new 25–29 age group.","event_date":"2024-01-17","evidence_status":"captured","id":"youth-unemployment-series-break","interpretation":"Comparisons across the break need a consistent population definition. A lower rate after the change does not by itself measure an improvement among the same people. NBS attributed the change to refining its labor-force statistics.","source_ids":["nbs-youth-suspension","nbs-youth-definition"],"source_urls":["https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/sjjd/202308/t20230815_1942020.html","https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfb/202401/t20240117_1946641.html"],"title":"The youth unemployment series changed its population definition"},{"capture_ids":["e4c15436e07ee1b019e3db64e99962480f2ab01c6b8a6aadcc5b8834b0e5931e","19d25d2a98f32132aad9db0bd5032aab89ff9aa78a4a5f0c325c894984863430"],"claim":"NBS revised the preliminary 2023 GDP estimate using the fifth economic census and a simultaneous change to the valuation of owner-occupied urban housing services.","event_date":"2024-12-27","evidence_status":"captured","id":"gdp-census-housing-revision","interpretation":"Separate the census revision from the accounting-method effect when comparing output vintages. This is a documented statistical revision; it is not itself evidence that output was fabricated.","source_ids":["nbs-gdp-revision","nbs-gdp-revision-method"],"source_urls":["https://www.stats.gov.cn/xxgk/sjfb/zxfb2020/202412/t20241227_1957915.html","https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/sjjd/202412/t20241227_1957914.html"],"title":"GDP revisions combine census evidence and a housing-services method change"},{"capture_ids":["9668d663e436fee3ef3fc383856bedb33453bad26448fad60945c1f7cbfd3b19","a91cf3d8686e9fd602e4bda409ad2c0d1973482a67ff37e64b19f0b7406120b3"],"claim":"NBS explains that survey unemployment concerns the labor force and that people neither searching nor available for work are outside that denominator. Its methodology distinguishes unemployment from hours and employment quality.","event_date":"2024-11-29","evidence_status":"captured","id":"unemployment-measurement-boundary","interpretation":"Read unemployment alongside hours, earnings, participation and working-age population. A stable headline alone cannot settle whether work is becoming more secure or better paid.","source_ids":["nbs-unemployment-definition","nbs-unemployment-coverage"],"source_urls":["https://www.stats.gov.cn/zs/tjws/zytjzbqs/tcsyl/202411/t20241115_1957491.html","https://www.stats.gov.cn/zs/tjws/zytjzbqs/tcsyl/202409/t20240910_1956360.html"],"title":"Unemployment rates leave job quality and inactive workers outside their headline"}],"schema":"palimpsest.china-publication-watch.v1","status":"partial"}
